---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Steward
    participant Page as Sites page<br/>/sites (also /admin/sites)
    participant Map as Site map<br/>components/map/SiteMap.tsx<br/>MapLibre GL
    participant Tiles as Protomaps<br/>api.protomaps.com
    participant Server as Server actions<br/>utils/supabase/queries.ts
    participant DB as Supabase<br/>PostgreSQL
    participant S3 as AWS S3

    Note over Steward,S3: Covers US 2.0.1 and 2.0.6. The map exists (#159, #161, #166, #167): a Cards View and Map View toggle on /sites,<br/>with the same toggle on /admin/sites. It draws protected_areas boundaries. The admin heat map in /admin/dashboard still uses Leaflet.<br/>Steps marked (Proposed) are not in the code today: the menu link, "View on map", GPX tracks and centring on a search match.

    opt Open the map from another page (2.0.1 AT3, Proposed)
        alt Open from the menu
            Steward->>Page: Select Map in HeaderDropdown (Proposed)
        else Open from a Site page
            Steward->>Page: Select "View on map" on /detail/[namesite] (Proposed)
        end
    end

    Steward->>Page: Open /sites and select "Map View"
    activate Page
    Page->>Map: Render SiteMap (loaded with dynamic import, no server render)
    activate Map
    alt NEXT_PUBLIC_PROTOMAPS_API_KEY is not set
        Map-->>Steward: Show "Map key not set" with the steps to add the key. No map is drawn.
    else The key is set
        Map->>Tiles: Get the map style and vector tiles (api.protomaps.com/styles/v5/light/en.json?key=...)
        Tiles-->>Map: Style and tiles
        Map-->>Steward: Draw the basemap. The view is limited to Alberta.
    end

    Note over Page,Server: The first time the map opens, the page loads the boundaries. They are not loaded again during the visit.
    Page->>Server: getProtectedAreaBoundaries()
    activate Server
    Server->>Server: requireApprovedCaller(): the session must have app_metadata.authenticated = true
    alt No valid session or account not approved
        Server-->>Page: Throw "You must be signed in to view site boundaries."
        Page-->>Steward: Show "Site boundaries could not load."
    else Access allowed
        Server->>DB: Read protected_areas (name, area_type, subtype, geometry and other fields)<br/>with the signed-in session. RLS lets signed-in users select.
        activate DB
        DB-->>Server: Boundaries
        Server->>DB: Read sites_pa.protected_area_id, is_active and the county (service role)
        DB-->>Server: The Site, county and status of each linked protected area
        deactivate DB
        Server->>Server: Join them. A protected area with no Site has no status.<br/>For a Steward, drop the boundaries of inactive Sites. An Admin gets them all.
        Server-->>Page: GeoJSON FeatureCollection
    end
    deactivate Server
    Page->>Map: boundaries (filtered, see below)
    Map-->>Steward: Draw each boundary as a filled polygon with an outline (AT1)
    Note right of Map: The map draws a polygon for every protected area, so a protected area with no Site also shows.<br/>The default status filter keeps Active Sites and areas with no Site, and hides inactive Sites.<br/>/sites has no status control. /admin/sites has one, so an Admin can show inactive Sites.

    opt Hover or click a boundary (2.0.1 AT4, 2.0.8)
        Steward->>Map: Move over a boundary
        Map-->>Steward: Highlight only that boundary. The previous one returns to normal.
        Steward->>Map: Click the boundary
        Map-->>Steward: Open a popup with the name, type and the other fields of the protected area
    end

    opt Zoom to a Site that has GPX tracks (2.0.1 AT2, Proposed)
        Map->>Server: getSiteTracks(siteId) (Proposed)
        activate Server
        Server->>DB: Read gpx_tracks rows of the Site (US 2.0.9)
        activate DB
        DB-->>Server: Track storage keys
        deactivate DB
        Server-->>Map: Short-lived presigned GET URLs
        deactivate Server
        Map->>S3: Get each GPX file
        S3-->>Map: GPX files
        Map-->>Steward: Draw tracks as lines in a style<br/>different from the boundary
    end

    opt Filter by county, type or subtype, and by status on /admin/sites (2.0.6 AT1, AT2)
        Steward->>Page: Select one or more values in the filters
        Page->>Page: filterBoundaryCollection() keeps the boundaries that match every filter.<br/>Inside one filter any selected value is enough. This runs in the browser.
        Page->>Map: Filtered boundaries
        Map->>Map: Replace the data of the GeoJSON source. The pan and zoom stay.
        Map-->>Steward: Show only matching boundaries. The page shows the count.
        Steward->>Page: Clear the filter
        Page->>Map: All boundaries again
        Map-->>Steward: Show all boundaries again (AT2). Inactive Sites stay hidden.
    end

    opt Search by name (2.0.6 AT3)
        Steward->>Page: Type in the search box
        Page->>Page: Keep the boundaries whose name, oc_name or county contains the text, ignoring case
        Page->>Map: Matching boundaries
        Map-->>Steward: Show only the matching boundaries
        opt Centre on the selected match (Proposed)
            Steward->>Map: Select a match
            Map-->>Steward: Centre the map on that Site (Proposed)
        end
    end
    deactivate Map
    deactivate Page

    Note over Steward,S3: Filter and search use the boundaries that are already loaded. They make no server call.<br/>Cards View uses getSitesOnline and the same search box and county filter.<br/>Open questions: GPX storage (see US 2.0.9) and the time window of tracks to show.
